WEBVTT

00:00:04.280 --> 00:00:11.280
"Funeral of Ryoko Nagaya"

00:00:17.690 --> 00:00:21.000
Please, Mr. Chairman, come inside.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:22.990
You too, Miss Sayaka.

00:00:27.140 --> 00:00:28.540
Ms. Nagaya...

00:00:29.070 --> 00:00:36.080
<i>Will the sky one day grow tired of</i>
<i>looking down and lose its blue color?</i>

00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:45.080
<i>There's just one blue sky over this</i>
<i>world rife with countless emotions</i>

00:00:49.060 --> 00:00:52.160
<i>The sound of the battle raging somewhere</i>

00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:55.100
<i>And the laughter right nearby</i>

00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:58.070
<i>You can never hear it all</i>

00:00:58.070 --> 00:01:00.670
<i>Because you have only one story</i>

00:01:00.670 --> 00:01:06.540
<i>Only this sky sees all at</i>
<i>once the sorrow and smiles</i>

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:12.520
<i>That simultaneously fall in different</i>
<i>places around this wide world</i>

00:01:12.520 --> 00:01:19.020
<i>Will the sky one day grow tired of</i>
<i>looking down and lose its blue color?</i>

00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:24.890
<i>How can it stay unchanging after</i>
<i>watching innumerable dramas?</i>

00:01:24.890 --> 00:01:31.130
<i>Even now everyone heads to his</i>
<i>own story without knowing a thing</i>

00:01:31.130 --> 00:01:39.370
<i>There's just one blue sky over this</i>
<i>world rife with countless emotions</i>

00:01:40.110 --> 00:01:50.540
<i>Wordlessly marking out</i>
<i>time longer than anyone's...</i>

00:02:22.120 --> 00:02:23.120
I don't get it!

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:24.090
Never mind!

00:02:24.090 --> 00:02:25.660
Thanks!

00:02:25.660 --> 00:02:26.640
Huh?

00:02:30.190 --> 00:02:31.630
What's this?

00:02:57.190 --> 00:02:58.180
It happened again...

00:02:59.690 --> 00:03:03.320
It's no good. Once again,
there were no witnesses.

00:03:05.290 --> 00:03:07.900
Well, not too many people
ride the trains at this hour.

00:03:07.900 --> 00:03:09.470
Hi there!

00:03:09.470 --> 00:03:11.170
Long time no see.

00:03:11.170 --> 00:03:12.900
What the hell, Muroto?

00:03:12.900 --> 00:03:16.210
If you've got a new book out,
just send it to the station.

00:03:16.210 --> 00:03:17.410
Not that I'll read it.

00:03:17.410 --> 00:03:20.410
No, no, that's not why I'm here today.

00:03:20.410 --> 00:03:22.580
I have a few questions about this incident.

00:03:22.580 --> 00:03:27.250
This is a murder. It's not
that supernatural stuff you like.

00:03:27.250 --> 00:03:29.990
Nonsense. I've heard the rumors, you know.

00:03:29.990 --> 00:03:33.390
What? Oh, that crap?

00:03:33.390 --> 00:03:36.380
Ah, that stuff about a song?

00:03:39.230 --> 00:03:42.530
It's a cursed song! The song of death!

00:03:42.530 --> 00:03:45.030
Whispers from the beyond.

00:03:45.030 --> 00:03:46.600
Cursed, eh?

00:03:46.600 --> 00:03:47.770
A song, huh?

00:03:47.770 --> 00:03:51.240
The whole internet is
talking about it right now, guys!

00:03:51.240 --> 00:03:56.910
On the nights the murders happen,
radios and TVs play this girl singing.

00:03:56.910 --> 00:04:01.380
You sure it's not one of those
ghost stories that used to be big,

00:04:01.380 --> 00:04:03.190
like Toilet Hanako or Teke-Teke?

00:04:03.190 --> 00:04:05.090
I'm telling you, this one is real!

00:04:05.090 --> 00:04:08.360
There's an actual recording
making its way around the Web!

00:04:08.360 --> 00:04:09.890
Scary!

00:04:09.890 --> 00:04:12.060
Kitamura, you're going to believe that?

00:04:12.060 --> 00:04:14.400
Come on, you don't believe me?!

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:17.230
A member of the Journalism Club
should be all over this!

00:04:17.230 --> 00:04:21.200
Don't we have an old boy
who specializes in this stuff?

00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:24.910
No way, no how! Muroto is the
shame of the Journalism Club!

00:04:24.910 --> 00:04:27.640
My idol is our senior Kaori Sanada.

00:04:27.640 --> 00:04:30.750
Plus, I'm not interested in silly gossip like that.

00:04:30.750 --> 00:04:32.480
"Silly gossip"?!

00:04:32.480 --> 00:04:35.110
That's just mean. Fine, then...

00:04:36.820 --> 00:04:38.590
Ghost stories?

00:04:38.590 --> 00:04:40.890
Do you have stuff like that on your planet, too?

00:04:40.890 --> 00:04:45.630
Sure we do. In Teledore on Renevia,
the ghost of a Kopper...

00:04:45.630 --> 00:04:47.460
Well?

00:04:47.460 --> 00:04:49.630
You downloaded it?

00:04:49.630 --> 00:04:50.600
Oh, no!

00:04:50.600 --> 00:04:55.640
Don't play us an unlucky song like that!

00:04:55.640 --> 00:04:58.010
Stop it!

00:04:58.010 --> 00:04:59.310
Nakasugi...

00:04:59.310 --> 00:05:01.940
Oh, Nakasugi! Over here, over here!

00:05:09.520 --> 00:05:12.190
Whoops.

00:05:12.190 --> 00:05:13.820
Are you okay?

00:05:17.430 --> 00:05:20.830
Who are you, little boy?
Where did you come from?

00:05:27.800 --> 00:05:30.640
Thank you. Are you from around here?

00:05:30.640 --> 00:05:33.440
But you shouldn't come into
our garden without permission.

00:05:33.440 --> 00:05:38.640
You don't have to worry.
You have a guardian angel.

00:05:52.030 --> 00:05:53.300
On to our next story.

00:05:53.300 --> 00:05:53.700
"Series of Murders on the Marunouchi Line"
On to our next story.

00:05:53.700 --> 00:05:56.670
The police still have no solid
clues in the series of daily murders

00:05:56.670 --> 00:05:57.700
"Series of Murders on the Marunouchi Line"

00:05:57.700 --> 00:06:00.540
centering around the Marunouchi subway line.

00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:02.540
The investigation seems to have bogged down.

00:06:02.540 --> 00:06:02.810
This is what they were talking
about in school today, right?

00:06:02.810 --> 00:06:05.510
According to the autopsy
reports made public today,

00:06:05.510 --> 00:06:06.510
Yeah.

00:06:06.510 --> 00:06:11.150
all four victims died of ruptured
organs due to thoracic compression.

00:06:11.150 --> 00:06:11.480
How could someone even do that?

00:06:11.480 --> 00:06:16.480
We're told the method and type of
weapon have yet to be determined.

00:06:17.320 --> 00:06:19.310
Hey, what's gotten into you?!

00:06:21.520 --> 00:06:25.090
Sheesh, these are so inconvenient...

00:06:25.090 --> 00:06:27.700
Why are you wearing your pinup girl clothes?!

00:06:27.700 --> 00:06:29.730
Don't sweat the details!

00:06:29.730 --> 00:06:32.360
I'm a little concerned about those murders.

00:06:36.410 --> 00:06:39.080
Um, who are you again?

00:06:39.080 --> 00:06:41.180
l-I, er...

00:06:41.180 --> 00:06:43.170
I've seen you somewhere...

00:06:44.750 --> 00:06:47.380
You're Shion Arita! Why are you here?!

00:06:51.850 --> 00:06:55.790
Yes, that's right. It's about the "cursed song."

00:06:55.790 --> 00:06:59.060
From what I heard today,
the way the victims died

00:06:59.060 --> 00:07:01.700
it was almost like they were
crushed to death by a gorilla.

00:07:01.700 --> 00:07:06.470
Yes. I think it'll be very
interesting to pursue this further.

00:07:06.470 --> 00:07:12.410
So... would you mind adding a
little extra to my research funds?

00:07:12.410 --> 00:07:14.380
Really?!

00:07:14.380 --> 00:07:18.780
Thanks, I'll write you
exactly what you're looking for!

00:07:18.780 --> 00:07:21.220
Right, goodbye.

00:07:21.220 --> 00:07:24.210
All right! I should be able to
make ends meet for a while now.

00:07:27.790 --> 00:07:29.780
I guess I'll have to let this one lie for a while.

00:07:32.800 --> 00:07:36.900
I'm Shion Arita, yessiree!

00:07:36.900 --> 00:07:39.140
You look so much like her!

00:07:39.140 --> 00:07:41.800
I'm flattered, yessiree.

00:07:41.800 --> 00:07:43.240
But man...

00:07:44.110 --> 00:07:48.480
I can't believe Tsutomu
managed to score a girlfriend,

00:07:48.480 --> 00:07:52.310
let alone that she's a dead ringer for Shion Arita!

00:07:52.310 --> 00:07:54.620
Say, do that one thing!

00:07:54.620 --> 00:07:58.850
Have a good day, Ma'am!

00:07:58.850 --> 00:08:00.620
You could be twins!

00:08:00.620 --> 00:08:03.330
Come on, just give her some excuse and escape!

00:08:03.330 --> 00:08:05.330
You want to go investigate the murders, right?

00:08:05.330 --> 00:08:07.660
I know, I know.

00:08:07.660 --> 00:08:09.870
Um, I need to be going now...

00:08:09.870 --> 00:08:13.200
No, no! The party's just getting started!

00:08:13.200 --> 00:08:15.190
Here! Drink up!

00:08:18.010 --> 00:08:20.780
O-Okay, I'll have just one before I go.

00:08:20.780 --> 00:08:22.370
Hey, now...

00:08:26.020 --> 00:08:31.350
Nice, nice! Way to chug it!

00:08:31.350 --> 00:08:34.320
Well, then...

00:08:34.320 --> 00:08:35.310
Huh?

00:08:36.990 --> 00:08:40.130
Whoa, are you okay?

00:08:40.130 --> 00:08:42.730
Yep, just fine...

00:08:42.730 --> 00:08:44.360
You're hopeless.

00:08:58.510 --> 00:08:59.500
No way!

00:09:40.720 --> 00:09:43.560
No!

00:09:54.700 --> 00:09:56.270
What, are you serious?

00:09:56.270 --> 00:09:57.910
I'm telling you, it's true!

00:09:57.910 --> 00:09:59.980
You sure it wasn't some mean prank?

00:09:59.980 --> 00:10:02.410
But there was another victim yesterday!

00:10:02.410 --> 00:10:04.550
And it was right around when I heard the song...

00:10:04.550 --> 00:10:07.220
Well, it doesn't have to be
the criminal who did it, right?

00:10:07.220 --> 00:10:09.750
Someone could have hijacked
the frequency to play that song.

00:10:09.750 --> 00:10:13.620
If it was really related to the murder,
wouldn't they say so on the news?

00:10:13.620 --> 00:10:18.130
The cops would never take
rumors like that seriously.

00:10:18.130 --> 00:10:21.500
If your big sister hadn't
gotten in my way yesterday...

00:10:21.500 --> 00:10:23.490
Whatever, you were so into it.

00:10:31.240 --> 00:10:36.350
Thanks to these crimes, we were
able identify a rough search area.

00:10:36.350 --> 00:10:38.080
We'll find it soon enough.

00:10:38.080 --> 00:10:39.850
I'm glad to hear it.

00:10:39.850 --> 00:10:42.520
I see specialists like you really
know how to get things done.

00:10:42.520 --> 00:10:47.960
But it has nothing to do with us.
You were developing it on your own.

00:10:47.960 --> 00:10:51.630
I know. Don't worry.

00:10:51.630 --> 00:10:55.620
This country's press are putty in my hands.

00:11:04.040 --> 00:11:06.780
Um...

00:11:06.780 --> 00:11:10.510
Excuse me, but did you know the victim?

00:11:10.510 --> 00:11:13.480
No...

00:11:13.480 --> 00:11:14.280
Shion Arita!

00:11:14.280 --> 00:11:16.290
N-No I'm not, nosiree!

00:11:16.290 --> 00:11:18.280
Yes you are!

00:11:19.390 --> 00:11:21.820
What's Muroto doing here?

00:11:25.490 --> 00:11:26.890
Hey!

00:11:29.130 --> 00:11:30.530
Sorry!

00:11:34.800 --> 00:11:37.200
You're not getting away!

00:11:51.890 --> 00:11:54.520
There's no place left to run, Shion Arita!

00:11:54.520 --> 00:11:58.030
Huh?

00:11:58.030 --> 00:12:01.530
Hey, if it isn't Muroto!

00:12:01.530 --> 00:12:07.600
Hmm... You're Hayamiya's
friend... Ichikawa? No... Mankawa?

00:12:07.600 --> 00:12:09.040
Senkawa.

00:12:09.040 --> 00:12:13.110
Right, Senkawa!
Anyway, Shion Arita was just here, wasn't she?

00:12:13.110 --> 00:12:14.610
Yeah, right!

00:12:14.610 --> 00:12:16.550
Nobody's been here.

00:12:16.550 --> 00:12:19.280
Huh? Really?

00:12:19.280 --> 00:12:21.350
You don't see anyone, do you?

00:12:21.350 --> 00:12:23.180
That's weird...

00:12:26.790 --> 00:12:27.220
"Soon Arriving in Shinjuku"

00:12:27.220 --> 00:12:32.090
Next stop, Shinjuku. Please exit to the left.

00:12:32.090 --> 00:12:33.730
Well, this is my stop.

00:12:33.730 --> 00:12:35.720
Hey, hold on!

00:12:43.740 --> 00:12:44.730
Hello?

00:12:51.780 --> 00:12:55.120
You too? Don't tell me there's another...

00:12:55.120 --> 00:12:56.950
What do we do, Birdy?

00:12:56.950 --> 00:12:58.580
Tuto!

00:13:01.560 --> 00:13:03.550
Hey! Senkawa!

00:13:14.240 --> 00:13:15.400
Is there something over here?

00:13:15.400 --> 00:13:17.910
Shh!

00:13:17.910 --> 00:13:19.740
I can hear singing.

00:13:37.260 --> 00:13:39.250
This is horrible...

00:13:41.000 --> 00:13:45.630
So do you think the Ryunka's
involved in this, Birdy?

00:13:45.630 --> 00:13:49.140
I can't be sure, but something about it bugs me.

00:13:49.140 --> 00:13:52.340
But would the Ryunka go
around murdering people?

00:13:52.340 --> 00:13:54.940
Well, everyone says it's hazardous,

00:13:54.940 --> 00:13:58.010
so it must be dangerous to Earthlings too.

00:13:58.010 --> 00:13:59.720
Maybe, but...

00:13:59.720 --> 00:14:03.350
Anyway, we have to find
anything suspicious and look into it!

00:14:03.350 --> 00:14:04.150
Whoa!

00:14:04.150 --> 00:14:07.120
Hmm? What is this?

00:14:07.120 --> 00:14:11.120
It's called an underground website.
It creeps me out, but...

00:14:12.560 --> 00:14:13.500
Huh?

00:14:13.500 --> 00:14:14.630
What is it?

00:14:14.630 --> 00:14:20.370
Say, don't these girls... look kind of alike?

00:14:20.370 --> 00:14:25.360
I see, so all the victims
have glasses and short hair.

00:14:33.320 --> 00:14:35.150
Oh, cut it out!

00:15:04.880 --> 00:15:07.620
Excuse me, Miss...

00:15:07.620 --> 00:15:11.520
Muroto! Wh-What are you doing here?!

00:15:11.520 --> 00:15:15.390
I thought the perp might
show up if I dressed like this.

00:15:15.390 --> 00:15:17.260
Wh-What is it?

00:15:17.260 --> 00:15:19.250
Don't tell me that's...

00:15:52.230 --> 00:15:53.960
Mama...

00:15:53.960 --> 00:15:56.330
What is this thing?!

00:15:56.330 --> 00:15:58.100
A marionette!

00:15:58.100 --> 00:15:59.930
Target confirmed.

00:16:02.800 --> 00:16:05.070
M-Mr. Chairman, please wait!

00:16:05.070 --> 00:16:07.340
Out of my way!

00:16:07.340 --> 00:16:11.750
What's this all about, Sasaki?! Explain it to me!

00:16:11.750 --> 00:16:13.850
M-Mr. Chairman?

00:16:13.850 --> 00:16:14.620
You're...

00:16:14.620 --> 00:16:19.620
Getting too excited is bad for
your health, Chairman Nakasugi.

00:16:19.620 --> 00:16:24.530
So Mr. Sasaki spilled the beans, eh?
He's so spineless.

00:16:24.530 --> 00:16:26.090
Shyamalan...

00:16:26.090 --> 00:16:30.300
The one behind the serial murders rocking Tokyo

00:16:30.300 --> 00:16:33.500
is a marionette escaped from these premises.

00:16:33.500 --> 00:16:35.000
A marionette?

00:16:35.000 --> 00:16:37.010
I'm sure you've heard

00:16:37.010 --> 00:16:42.210
that the marionettes developed
here are no mere nursing robots.

00:16:42.210 --> 00:16:45.650
No one ever told me they were for military use!

00:16:45.650 --> 00:16:50.020
Did you really think I would make nursing robots?

00:16:50.020 --> 00:16:52.650
How much money do you
think I invested in this lab?!

00:17:01.800 --> 00:17:08.840
Mama... Locked on to target. Mama...

00:17:08.840 --> 00:17:11.310
Mama...

00:17:11.310 --> 00:17:13.140
Delete target.

00:17:14.710 --> 00:17:16.980
Oh no...

00:17:16.980 --> 00:17:17.850
Mama.

00:17:17.850 --> 00:17:19.580
This thing is...

00:17:19.580 --> 00:17:21.010
Delete.

00:17:23.690 --> 00:17:25.190
Its mother?!

00:17:25.190 --> 00:17:28.360
These women have the same
characteristics as Chief Nagaya.

00:17:28.360 --> 00:17:30.490
Did she program it?

00:17:30.490 --> 00:17:36.100
Yes. She wanted to produce
reactions of clinginess and adoration.

00:17:36.100 --> 00:17:39.030
So she succeeded in analyzing the M Program?

00:17:39.030 --> 00:17:42.540
Yes, though there were a few bugs.

00:17:42.540 --> 00:17:46.940
Going along with your stupid
dreams won't get us through in life.

00:17:46.940 --> 00:17:50.680
Your men here understand better than you do.

00:17:50.680 --> 00:17:56.450
The M Program that enabled marionettes
to act spontaneously was a black box.

00:17:56.450 --> 00:17:58.750
But now we've solved the riddle.

00:17:58.750 --> 00:18:02.420
Even the military labs of a certain
country couldn't tinker with it.

00:18:02.420 --> 00:18:06.230
This has proven how
talented your subordinates are.

00:18:06.230 --> 00:18:09.930
Where did you get the basic
design for that marionette?!

00:18:09.930 --> 00:18:12.370
You don't need to know that.

00:18:20.410 --> 00:18:24.400
Wow, you've memorized the song I taught you!

00:18:30.090 --> 00:18:34.220
What a good girl, to learn Mama's song.

00:18:34.220 --> 00:18:35.660
Mama?

00:18:35.660 --> 00:18:40.830
That's right. I'm Mama.
Sorry it took so long to tune your eyes.

00:18:40.830 --> 00:18:43.660
I love you. I'll give you a hug.

00:18:47.300 --> 00:18:50.500
I love you too, Mama. I'll give you a hug.

00:19:28.380 --> 00:19:30.110
You did it, Birdy.

00:19:30.110 --> 00:19:34.280
Maybe if you check this thing out,
you can find a clue.

00:19:34.280 --> 00:19:36.490
Hey, are you listening?

00:19:36.490 --> 00:19:40.110
Oh, sorry. You're right. Okay, I'll bring it...

00:19:44.360 --> 00:19:45.490
What was that?!

00:19:45.490 --> 00:19:46.480
Shit!

00:19:49.330 --> 00:19:50.730
A Marker?

00:19:56.840 --> 00:19:58.040
They got away.

00:19:58.040 --> 00:20:00.140
Who was that?

00:20:00.140 --> 00:20:02.740
That... was someone from the Federation.

00:20:06.250 --> 00:20:08.880
The next train's the last one, little lady.

00:20:13.560 --> 00:20:14.990
Thank you.

00:20:15.920 --> 00:20:19.330
You lost sight of her? What do you mean by that?

00:20:19.330 --> 00:20:22.230
I just got word from one of my men.

00:20:22.230 --> 00:20:25.400
Apparently she suddenly
stopped emitting any signal.

00:20:25.400 --> 00:20:28.840
Looks like it'll be tough to secure
her before the end of the day.

00:20:32.570 --> 00:20:34.570
What happened? What was that sound?

00:20:36.610 --> 00:20:39.010
I found the marionette.

00:20:39.010 --> 00:20:40.000
What?

00:20:48.720 --> 00:20:54.460
Playing with dolls is fine and all,
but make sure you clean up afterward.

00:20:54.460 --> 00:21:00.700
Or else someone will beat you
to the treasure you're looking for.

00:21:00.700 --> 00:21:03.240
Who are you?

00:21:03.240 --> 00:21:05.540
A guardian angel.

00:21:05.540 --> 00:21:08.080
I don't believe in those.

00:21:08.080 --> 00:21:09.910
Neither do I.

00:21:27.430 --> 00:21:29.260
Want to be friends?

00:21:38.240 --> 00:21:39.230
This feels good...

00:21:42.280 --> 00:21:43.810
<i>Let's go! Have a good time!</i>

00:21:43.810 --> 00:21:46.980
<i>A peaceful, happy</i>
<i>cheek-to-cheek time for everybody</i>

00:21:46.980 --> 00:21:52.980
<i>Put your hands, let's become one now</i>

00:21:59.290 --> 00:22:01.260
<i>Come on, make some noise,</i>
<i>clap your hands, slap slap!</i>

00:22:01.260 --> 00:22:03.330
<i>Lift your hands, clap your hands, slap slap!</i>

00:22:03.330 --> 00:22:05.430
<i>Everyone has their worries</i>

00:22:05.430 --> 00:22:07.700
<i>Given they're neverending,</i>
<i>what'll you do from here on out?</i>

